| 10 | Implicit mixed disallowed everywhere |
```

--------------------------------

### Constructing PHPStan Types

Source: https://github.com/phpstan/phpstan-src/blob/2.2.x/_autodocs/09-api-quick-reference.md

Demonstrates the creation of various PHPStan type instances, including simple types, object types, unions, intersections, and generic objects.

```php
use PHPStan\Type\ObjectType;
use PHPStan\Type\TypeCombinator;
use PHPStan\Type\Generic\GenericObjectType;
use PHPStan\Type\Generic\TemplateTypeMap;

// Simple types
$string = new StringType();
$int = new IntegerType();
$bool = new BooleanType();

// Object type
$object = new ObjectType('MyClass');

// Union
$union = TypeCombinator::union(
    new StringType(),
    new NullType(),
);

// Intersection
$intersection = TypeCombinator::intersection(
    new ObjectType('Foo'),
    new ObjectType('Stringable'),
);

// Generic object
$templateTypes = new TemplateTypeMap(['T' => new IntegerType()]);
$generic = new GenericObjectType('List', $templateTypes);
```

### Type System > TypeCombinator

Source: https://github.com/phpstan/phpstan-src/blob/2.2.x/_autodocs/02-type-system.md

The TypeCombinator class in PHPStan is used for creating UnionType and IntersectionType instances. It automatically normalizes types, such as simplifying `mixed | int` to `mixed` or correctly flattening unions and handling invalid intersections like `int & string` which results in `never`.

